# The variate domain is `reals`, not `nonnegreals`: §09 gives ContinuedPoisson
# the domain `reals` with the support `nonnegreals`, and the point grid scores
# below zero on purpose to reach the off-support branch.
#
# ContinuedPoisson is a `%finite` measure, so `lawof` refuses it (§04: an
# unnormalized measure is not its own law). The density is reached the way
# HistFactory's converter output reaches it, through `functionof` +
# `likelihoodof`.
hep = standard_module("particle-physics", "0.1")
x = elementof(reals)
aux = functionof(hep.ContinuedPoisson(rate = 4.5))
aux_lik = likelihoodof(aux, x)
